    "summary": "The doc still says applying the function twice gives the same result, but `layer_checker_props` now changes `entry.props` itself (it moves structural notables into props before the merge), so a second call sees a different entry.",
    "failure_scenario": "Call it twice on an entry whose structural layer has a notable member the checker answered, with no merge and `move_notable` in between. The first call moves `className` into `entry.props`. The second call's `of_entry` filter (`!listed.contains_key`) drops `className`, so its `notable` list no longer names it. `move_notable` then never moves it back, and `className` ends up as an ordinary prop. The existing double-apply test only uses `on*` props, which are not notable, so it does not catch this."
